TEXT 64 96 Left 2 ;Q1a RTC SCL: FPGA drives it low at 5.0 ms
TEXT 448 96 Left 2 ;Q1b RTC SDA: the RTC pulls low at 2.5 ms (asleep) and 5.5 ms (awake)
TEXT 832 96 Left 2 ;Q2a push button: pressed 1-2 ms (asleep) and 6-7 ms (awake)
TEXT 1216 96 Left 2 ;Q2b RTC alarm: 3-3.5 ms (asleep) and 8-8.5 ms (awake)
TEXT 64 496 Left 2 ;Sources: 3V3_AO always on; +3V3 (p3v3) switches on at 4 ms. The ctl_* sources drive ideal open-drain pull-downs (ODRV).
TEXT 64 688 Left 2 !.tran 0 10m 0 1u
TEXT 64 720 Left 2 !.model NX2N7002 VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto=1.6 Rd=0.4 Rs=0.4 Rb=0.5 Kp=0.35 Lambda=0.01 Cgdmax=15p Cgdmin=2p Cgs=20p Cjo=20p Is=5e-12 N=1.1 Rds=1e9 Vds=60)
TEXT 64 752 Left 2 !.model ODRV VDMOS(Vto=1 Kp=5 Rd=2 Rs=2)\n.model DCLAMP D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=5 Cjo=2p)
TEXT 64 816 Left 2 ;th_power: isolation between the FPGA (switched +3V3 = p3v3) and the always-on domain (p3v3_ao). One N-FET per line: gate on the switched rail,\n;source on the FPGA side (bottom line), drain on the always-on side (top line); each side has its own pull-up to its own rail. Dclamp is the ESD diode of the FPGA pin.\n;1. Both high: Vgs = 0, channel off, each pull-up holds its own side.   2. FPGA side low: Vgs = 3.3 V, channel on, the AO side follows (5.0 ms, SCL).\n;3. AO side low: the body diode (anode = source) drags the FPGA side to ~0.7 V, then Vgs > Vth and the channel takes it to ~0 V: a two-step edge, zoom 5.5 ms on V(rtc_sda).\n;4. Rail off (before 4 ms): gate 0 V, channel off; drain 3.3 V, source 0 V, body diode reverse-biased: the AO side works (button, alarm) and nothing flows into the dead FPGA.\n;Plot V(pb_n_ao) V(pb_n) V(p3v3) first, then V(rtc_sda_ao) V(rtc_sda), and I(Dclamp2a) to see that the clamp current stays zero with the rail off.
